      "Low physical activity and excess body fat, particularly visceral fat around the abdomen, also lower testosterone through a well documented mechanism. Fat tissue contains an enzyme called aromatase that converts testosterone into estrogen, so more visceral fat generally means lower circulating testosterone.",
