      "Small, consistent gestures of affection matter more than people expect. A hand on the back while passing in the kitchen, real eye contact during a conversation instead of glancing at a phone, a few uninterrupted minutes of actual conversation each day. These rebuild trust and closeness gradually, often faster than one grand gesture ever could.",
      "Resentment is worth naming honestly, because it quietly kills desire more than almost anything else. Unresolved disagreements about chores, parenting, or feeling unappreciated tend to show up in the bedroom eventually, even when neither partner consciously connects the two.",
