      "As estrogen rises heading toward ovulation, mucus typically becomes cloudy and sticky, then progressively more clear, stretchy, and slippery. At peak fertility, right before ovulation, it's often compared to raw egg white, and this texture actually supports sperm survival and movement through the cervix.",
      "After ovulation, rising progesterone causes mucus to become thick, sticky, or disappear again fairly quickly, usually within a day or two. This shift back to dryness is one of the clearest signs that ovulation has already happened.",
